<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zechariah of Israel</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 753 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century-bce">8th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zechariah was king of Israel for six months around 753 BCE, the son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jeroboam-ii">Jeroboam II</a> and the last ruler of the dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jehu">Jehu</a>. According to the Bible he was murdered in public by Shallum, who took the throne. His death began a period of rapid and violent changes of ruler that lasted until the Assyrian conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samaria">Samaria</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zechariah-of-israel.jpg" alt="Zechariah of Israel" width="320" height="324" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Published by Guillaume Rouille (1518?-1589) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Zechariah_of_Israel.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
